### API Monitor — ready-to-run requests
### VS Code "REST Client" (humao.rest-client): click "Send Request" above each block, top to bottom.
### Named requests (`# @name`) feed later ones, e.g. {{login.response.body.$.data.access_token}}.
### Values match .env.example (local only). Start the stack first: docker compose up --build

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3001
@ingestKey = dev-only-ingest-key-0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef
@adminEmail = admin@example.com
@adminPassword = dev-only-Admin-2026
@origin = http://localhost:3000

############################################################################
# 1. Health and meta
############################################################################

### Liveness
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/live

### Readiness (database + Redis)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/ready

### Full health report (AI circuit states, simulator)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Public runtime info
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/meta

### OpenAPI document (Swagger UI lives at /docs)
GET {{baseUrl}}/docs/openapi.json

############################################################################
# 2. Ingest the assignment PDF example
############################################################################

### POST /monitor with the ingest key (also works anonymously when DEMO_MODE=true)
# @name ingestPdf
POST {{baseUrl}}/monitor
Content-Type: application/json
x-ingest-key: {{ingestKey}}

[
  { "api_name": "PatientDataAPI", "response_time_ms": 1200, "status_code": 200, "records_returned": 50 },
  { "api_name": "AppointmentAPI", "response_time_ms": 5500, "status_code": 500, "records_returned": 0 }
]

### Same payload again → still one alert, occurrence_count 2
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/monitor
Content-Type: application/json
x-ingest-key: {{ingestKey}}

[
  { "api_name": "PatientDataAPI", "response_time_ms": 1200, "status_code": 200, "records_returned": 50 },
  { "api_name": "AppointmentAPI", "response_time_ms": 5500, "status_code": 500, "records_returned": 0 }
]

### Wrapped batch with a source label and an Idempotency-Key (send twice → replayed)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/monitor
Content-Type: application/json
x-ingest-key: {{ingestKey}}
Idempotency-Key: 6f9619ff-8b86-4011-b42d-00c04fc964ff

{
  "logs": [
    { "api_name": "LabResultsAPI", "response_time_ms": 2600, "status_code": 200, "records_returned": 18 },
    { "api_name": "EHRIntegrationAPI", "response_time_ms": 480, "status_code": 200 }
  ],
  "source": "webhook"
}

############################################################################
# 3. Log in (sets the httpOnly refresh cookie; keep the access token in memory)
############################################################################

### Login
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{adminEmail}}", "password": "{{adminPassword}}" }

###
@token = {{login.response.body.$.data.access_token}}

### Current user and permissions
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Rotate the refresh cookie (needs the cookie from login + an allowed Origin)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/refresh
Origin: {{origin}}

############################################################################
# 4. Alerts
############################################################################

### Active alerts (assignment path)
# @name listAlerts
GET {{baseUrl}}/alerts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
@alertId = {{listAlerts.response.body.$.data[0].id}}

### Filtered, paginated
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/alerts?status=ALL&severity=CRITICAL&sort=severity&limit=10&offset=0
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Summary (dashboard)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/alerts/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Detail with the last 20 samples
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/alerts/{{alertId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Realtime: get a single-use stream ticket (60 s)
# @name ticket
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/alerts/stream-ticket
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Open the SSE stream (REST Client shows the first chunk; use `curl -N` to watch it live)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/alerts/stream?ticket={{ticket.response.body.$.data.ticket}}

### Re-run AI text generation (202)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/alerts/{{alertId}}/regenerate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Resolve
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/alerts/{{alertId}}/resolve
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "note": "Restarted the scheduler pods" }

### Resolved alerts
GET {{baseUrl}}/alerts?status=RESOLVED
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

############################################################################
# 5. Ingestion helpers
############################################################################

### Allowlisted sample files
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/monitor/static/files
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Ingest a sample file (logged-in user required)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/monitor/static
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "file": "edge-cases.json" }

### Pull 10 live items from the simulator and ingest them
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/monitor/fetch-live
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "count": 10 }

### Recent ingestion runs
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/monitor/runs?limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

############################################################################
# 6. Simulator (proxied, RBAC applies)
############################################################################

### Scenarios
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/simulator/scenarios
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Outage burst → one alert, occurrence_count 25, one email
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/simulator/scenarios/outage-burst
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Escalation → WARNING then CRITICAL, escalation email
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/simulator/scenarios/escalation
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Start a stream (auto-stops after STREAM_MAX_DURATION_MS)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/simulator/stream/start
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "interval_ms": 2000, "batch_size": 10 }

### Stream status
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/simulator/stream/status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Stop the stream
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/simulator/stream/stop
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

############################################################################
# 7. Monitored APIs and thresholds
############################################################################

### Monitored APIs with last-hour stats
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/apis
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Per-API thresholds (both null = back to defaults)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/apis/LabResultsAPI/thresholds
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "latency_warning_ms": 3000, "latency_critical_ms": 8000 }

############################################################################
# 8. Users (admins only; there is no public registration)
############################################################################

### List users
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create a manager (reserved role: can log in and call /auth/me only)
# @name createManager
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "manager-{{$timestamp}}@example.com", "password": "a-long-manager-password", "role": "MANAGER" }

### Log in as the manager
# @name managerLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{createManager.response.body.$.data.email}}", "password": "a-long-manager-password" }

###
@managerToken = {{managerLogin.response.body.$.data.access_token}}

### The manager can read /auth/me (permissions: [])…
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}

### …and change their own password (returns a fresh session; other sessions end)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/change-password
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "current_password": "a-long-manager-password", "new_password": "a-brand-new-password-2026" }

### Deactivate that manager (ends their sessions immediately)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/{{createManager.response.body.$.data.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "is_active": false }

############################################################################
# 9. Audit trail
############################################################################

### Latest security events
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/audit-logs?limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Only failed logins
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/audit-logs?action=auth.login.failure
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

############################################################################
# 9b. Alert-email settings
############################################################################

### Who receives alert emails, and the SMTP setup the server uses
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/settings/notifications
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Change the recipients (takes effect for the next alert email)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/settings/notifications
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "alert_email_to": ["oncall@example.com"] }

### Send a test email to the saved recipients (or pass "to")
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/settings/notifications/test
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

############################################################################
# 10. Session end
############################################################################

### Logout (revokes the refresh token, clears the cookie)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/logout
Origin: {{origin}}
